      "block_id": "2605.18130_p10_b21",
      "text": "suppressing optimization noise from poor prompts. Ultimately,\nthe joint integration of all components (V1+V2+V3) achieves\nthe optimal diagnostic equilibrium (Accuracy 89.83%, AUC\n92.84%, F1 90.32%) without degrading segmentation quality\n(mDSC 0.9158). This confirms that our approach is not a\nnaive prompt ensemble, but a cohesive, classification-aware\nframework that successfully balances spatial stability, semantic\ncorrectness, and training regularization.\n",
